{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"interface segregation principle interface segregation principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","fileName":"Interface Segregation Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Interface Segregation Principle","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Software Design Principles]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"interface segregation principle interface segregation principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","fileName":"Interface Segregation Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Interface Segregation Principle","heading":"Interface Segregation Principle","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The interface segregation principle keeps a contract focused on operations its consumers actually need. A read-only inventory command should depend on a read interface, while a command that changes quantity depends on a write interface; neither needs to see an unrelated method. Smaller role-specific interfaces reduce coupling and make tests and future refactoring more precise.\n\nSmall capability-focused interfaces prevent implementers from depending on or supplying members they do not need. A class can combine several applicable interfaces instead of inheriting one broad contract containing unrelated responsibilities.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"interface segregation principle interface segregation principle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Interface Segregation Principle.md","fileName":"Interface Segregation Principle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Interface Segregation Principle","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Software Design Principles","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}